Subject: [PATCH] package: give atriumd a manual and name its debuginfo package
Origin: other, Peios catalogue qualification review
Upstream-Status: Pending [payload manual and conventional debug package name]

Two payload-lint failures against atrium 0.0.27.

usr/sbin/atriumd shipped without a manual page. Add a source-grounded section 8
manual describing the daemon's actual interface, install it compressed
deterministically, and verify the staged payload against the source text in the
existing gate. The two helpers under usr/libexec are not on a PATH and need
none.

The debug package was named dev.peios.atrium-debuginfo, but the package that
ships the executables is dev.peios.atrium-core, so pekit's {{name}}-debuginfo
rule found nothing for their debug data. Rename it to
dev.peios.atrium-core-debuginfo, matching netd, timed, trustd and peinit, and
repoint the debugsource dependency. No payload moves: the same
usr/lib/debug/** is carried under the conventional name.

diff --git a/man/atriumd.8 b/man/atriumd.8
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7a807bf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/man/atriumd.8
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+.TH ATRIUMD 8 "" "Peios" "System Administration"
+.SH NAME
+atriumd \- Peios web session host
+.SH SYNOPSIS
+.B atriumd
+.RB [ \-\-unrestricted ]
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+.B atriumd
+is the single privileged process of Atrium, the browser-delivered interactive
+session. It runs as SYSTEM because originating a logon requires it: the
+authority's logon socket admits SYSTEM alone. Everything else is deliberately
+placed on the far side of that privilege.
+.PP
+The daemon does three things.
+It spawns
+.IR /usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-server ,
+the network-facing half, under a copy of its own token with every privilege
+deleted, joined to it by a single socketpair.
+On the server's behalf it holds PGSS Logon conversations with the authority and
+keeps the resulting tokens in a session table.
+For each successful logon it submits one
+.I /usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-session
+to peinit as that principal (PSPU \(sc7) and hands the server the socket that
+reaches it.
+.PP
+.B atriumd
+never parses HTTP, never impersonates, and never forks as any identity but its
+own. Nothing that listens on a port runs as SYSTEM. It reads no registry
+configuration of its own; its only configuration is the service definition that
+starts it.
+.SH OPTIONS
+.TP
+.B \-\-unrestricted
+Skip the token work, for a development host without KACS. The server and every
+session then run as this process's own identity. This is a development switch,
+not a deployment mode; the daemon logs a warning saying so on every start.
+.SH STARTUP AND SUPERVISION
+The installed service definition runs
+.B atriumd
+at the boot trigger as SYSTEM, requires lpsd, and uses Notify readiness: the
+daemon sends
+.B READY=1
+to the socket named by
+.B NOTIFY_SOCKET
+once atrium-server has been spawned. Because the listener belongs to the
+server, a bind failure appears as the server exiting and
+.B atriumd
+exiting after it. Its restart policy is Always, which is the recovery path for
+everything: sessions do not survive an
+.B atriumd
+restart, by current decision.
+.PP
+A logout stops that session's peinit job. peinit closes an idle jobs connection
+after 30 seconds (PSPU \(sc7.A), so a connection is opened per operation rather
+than held.
+.SH ENVIRONMENT
+.TP
+.B NOTIFY_SOCKET
+Readiness datagram socket. When unset, no readiness notification is sent.
+.TP
+.B ATRIUM_JOBS_SOCKET
+Overrides the peinit jobs socket, which is
+.I /run/services/peinit/jobs.sock
+by default. Intended for testing against a disposable jobs endpoint.
+.SH FILES
+.TP
+.I /usr/sbin/atriumd
+This daemon.
+.TP
+.I /usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-server
+The network-facing half, spawned unprivileged. It owns the listening socket,
+which is 0.0.0.0:8080 unless
+.B ATRIUM_LISTEN
+overrides it.
+.TP
+.I /usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-session
+The per-principal session host, one submitted to peinit per logon.
+.TP
+.I /usr/share/regim/atriumd-service.reg
+Service definition seed. It is inert until an image names it in its registry
+autoapply configuration.
+.SH DIAGNOSTICS
+Messages are written to standard error, which peinit forwards to the log
+collector, and are mirrored to
+.I /dev/kmsg
+so that
+.BR dmesg (1)
+and the serial console find them on an image without a collector. A machine
+where kmsg cannot be opened still runs.
+.PP
+Failure to start atrium-server, loss of the control socket, or the server
+exiting are all fatal and exit with status 1.
+.SH SEE ALSO
+.BR peinit (8)
+.PP
+Running this executable on a development host does not constitute a service
+test; it requires a configured Peios system with the authority, lpsd and peinit
+present.
diff --git a/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-core-debuginfo.package.pekit.toml b/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-core-debuginfo.package.pekit.toml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4d45266
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-core-debuginfo.package.pekit.toml
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Named for the package whose objects it carries, as every other Peios recipe
+# names its debug packages: atrium-core ships all three executables, so their
+# debug data belongs in atrium-core-debuginfo.
+
+[package]
+name        = "dev.peios.atrium-core-debuginfo"
+description = "Atrium runtime debugging symbols"
+
+[dependencies]
+"dev.peios.atrium-core" = "{{version}}"
+
+[files]
+"@source:LICENSE"       = "usr/share/licenses/dev.peios.atrium-core-debuginfo/LICENSE"
+":usr/lib/debug/**"     = "usr/lib/debug"
diff --git a/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-core.package.pekit.toml b/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-core.package.pekit.toml
index 91dfdb6..f0883bf 100644
--- a/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-core.package.pekit.toml
+++ b/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-core.package.pekit.toml
@@ -21,3 +21,4 @@ description = "Peios web session host runtime"
 ":usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-server"            = "usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-server"
 ":usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-session"           = "usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-session"
 ":usr/share/regim/atriumd-service.reg"         = "usr/share/regim/atriumd-service.reg"
+":usr/share/man/man8/atriumd.8.gz"             = "usr/share/man/man8/atriumd.8.gz"
diff --git a/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-debuginfo.package.pekit.toml b/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-debuginfo.package.pekit.toml
deleted file mode 100644
index d4ab3f7..0000000
--- a/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-debuginfo.package.pekit.toml
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,10 +0,0 @@
-[package]
-name        = "dev.peios.atrium-debuginfo"
-description = "Atrium runtime debugging symbols"
-
-[dependencies]
-"dev.peios.atrium-core" = "{{version}}"
-
-[files]
-"@source:LICENSE"       = "usr/share/licenses/dev.peios.atrium-debuginfo/LICENSE"
-":usr/lib/debug/**"     = "usr/lib/debug"
diff --git a/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-debugsource.package.pekit.toml b/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-debugsource.package.pekit.toml
index cbd041c..23ffb4f 100644
--- a/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-debugsource.package.pekit.toml
+++ b/packages.pekit/dev.peios.atrium-debugsource.package.pekit.toml
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ architecture = "noarch"
 description  = "Atrium runtime debug sources"
 
 [dependencies]
-"dev.peios.atrium-debuginfo" = "{{version}}"
+"dev.peios.atrium-core-debuginfo" = "{{version}}"
 
 [files]
 "@source:LICENSE"       = "usr/share/licenses/dev.peios.atrium-debugsource/LICENSE"
diff --git a/pekit.toml b/pekit.toml
index 6330dca..528d8cc 100644
--- a/pekit.toml
+++ b/pekit.toml
@@ -114,6 +114,22 @@ mkdir -p "$PEKIT_OUT/usr/share/regim"
 cp "$SRC/registry.d/atriumd-service.reg" "$PEKIT_OUT/usr/share/regim/atriumd-service.reg"
 test -f "$PEKIT_OUT/usr/share/regim/atriumd-service.reg"
 
+# The one program in a binary directory is the one that needs a manual; the
+# two helpers under libexec are not on anyone's PATH. Compressed here without
+# an extra build tool dependency, and deterministically: no name, no mtime.
+python3 - "$SRC" "$PEKIT_OUT" <<'PY_MAN'
+import gzip, os, pathlib, sys
+source, output = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])
+data = (source / "man" / "atriumd.8").read_bytes()
+target = output / "usr/share/man/man8/atriumd.8.gz"
+target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+with target.open("wb") as raw:
+    with gzip.GzipFile(filename="", mode="wb", fileobj=raw, mtime=0) as stream:
+        stream.write(data)
+os.chmod(target, 0o644)
+PY_MAN
+test -s "$PEKIT_OUT/usr/share/man/man8/atriumd.8.gz"
+
 # Conventional build-ID indexed symbols and the exact sources named by their
 # DWARF. Statically linked vendored crates are part of these executables, so
 # their referenced sources live in Atrium's debugsource package too.
@@ -240,6 +256,21 @@ rm -f "$FAKE_JOBS" "$PEKIT_OUT/fake-peinit.log"
 SRC=$(pwd -P)
 PEKIT_OUT="$PEKIT_MAIN_OUT"
 APPS="$PEKIT_OUT/usr/share/atrium/apps"
+
+# The staged manual must be the source text, compressed reproducibly.
+python3 - "$SRC" "$PEKIT_OUT" <<'PY_MAN'
+import gzip, pathlib, sys
+source, output = map(pathlib.Path, sys.argv[1:])
+original = (source / "man" / "atriumd.8").read_bytes()
+staged = output / "usr/share/man/man8/atriumd.8.gz"
+assert gzip.decompress(staged.read_bytes()) == original, "staged manual differs from source"
+assert original.startswith(b'.TH ATRIUMD 8 '), "manual has no section 8 title line"
+# No stored name and no timestamp, so two builds of one source agree byte for byte.
+header = staged.read_bytes()[:8]
+assert not header[3] & 0x08, "manual gzip stores a filename"
+assert header[4:8] == b"\0\0\0\0", "manual gzip stores a timestamp"
+PY_MAN
+
 # Fail closed on the properties expected from the distribution Rust policy.
 for elf in \
   "$PEKIT_OUT/usr/sbin/atriumd" \
